From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ilya Nikolaevskiy <ilnik@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 05:31:12 -0800
Subject: [DirectShow] Release the capture filter before the sink on teardown

~VideoCaptureDeviceWin() assumed that once IMediaControl::Stop() and the pin disconnections had returned, the upstream capture filter no longer called into the sink. That doesn't hold for every filter: some return from Stop() without joining their streaming thread, and only join it when their last COM reference is released. Since |input_sink_pin_| was destroyed before |capture_filter_|, such a thread could still call into the freed SinkInputPin.

Release the capture filter and the other graph interfaces explicitly, before |input_sink_pin_| and |sink_filter_|, and declare the sink members first so that implicit destruction follows the same order. Release the filter graph after the capture filter, since the graph owns any intermediate filters (e.g. the AVI decompressor inserted for HDYC) that the capture filter's thread can call into. This relies on |capture_filter_| holding the last reference to the capture filter; the destructor documents that.

This fix is based on AI-generated fix.

Fixed: 583188056
Change-Id: I2807455bd3096254312cc7ae5ab06bc735fec1fd
